Turen Image Inspect is a bounded offline image/container metadata-inspection
WebAssembly module.

It directly uses two permissively licensed crates:

- kamadak-exif 0.6.1 (https://github.com/kamadak/exif-rs), BSD-2-Clause,
  for EXIF/TIFF tag parsing.
- image 0.25.10 (https://github.com/image-rs/image), MIT OR Apache-2.0,
  for bounded PNG/JPEG pixel decode inside image_pixel_stats only. Its PNG
  path uses png 0.18.1 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) and its JPEG path uses
  zune-jpeg (MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR Zlib).

All format structure walkers (PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, WebP, TIFF, ICO, and the
ISO BMFF/AVIF box table) are original Turen code and perform no decoding of
pixel payloads.

The compiled module also embeds other permissively licensed crates.io
dependencies (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, Unicode, or Zlib licensed; see
Cargo.lock for the full closure) and Rust standard-library components
distributed under Apache-2.0 or MIT.

Turen added the bounded WebAssembly wrapper, the anomaly and text-extraction
surfaces, and the packaging.
